course: dictionary
lesson: 9216
title: Solution: a fix, an answer, or a mix
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A solution is a way to solve a problem, or the answer to a puzzle. The words around it give you the clue. «The solution to the maths puzzle took her ten minutes.» Puzzle and maths tell you that solution means the answer.
explain: «We talked until we found a solution to the argument.» An argument is a problem between people, so a solution is a way to deal with it. Check by swapping in your meaning: "a way to deal with the argument" still makes sense.
explain: Science uses the word in a special way. «The sugar plus the water make a solution» means the sugar has dissolved, so you cannot see it any more, but it is still there. The solid is the solute and the liquid is the solvent.
fact: A solution is a way to solve a problem.
fact: In science, a solution is a liquid with something dissolved in it, like salt water.
fact: «Show the steps of your solution» means show how you worked out your answer.
fact: When sugar dissolves in water, the sugar is the solute and the water is the solvent.
fact: A dissolved solid is still there: a solution weighs as much as the water and the solid together.
exercise: In science, what is a solution? | *A liquid with something dissolved in it | A sweet cake | A cold, hard rock | A solid that has melted into a gas
exercise: «She found a solution to the argument.» What does solution mean here? | *A way to deal with the problem | A kind of puzzle box | A long, boring speech | A liquid in a glass
exercise: When sugar dissolves in water, what is the solute? | The glass | The water | *The sugar | The steam
test: «Show the steps of your solution.» In this maths sentence, what does solution mean? | A liquid in a bottle | A way to make a friend | A kind of sugar | *The answer you worked out
test: Ravi says salt water weighs less after the salt dissolves. Is he right? | Yes, the salt floats away | *No, a solution weighs as much as the water and the salt together | Yes, the salt disappears so it weighs nothing | No, salt water has no weight at all
exam: Which meaning fits «Squash is a solution: more water makes it more dilute»? | *A liquid with something dissolved in it | A way to end an argument | A type of puzzle | A cold, hard block of ice
